# Agentforce — Apex Payload Class Rules

Apex classes that serve as Lightning Type data contracts must follow these rules exactly.

## Access modifier

Use `public class` — NOT `global`. Global breaks the Agentforce type binding.

```java
// ✅ GOOD
public class MyCardOutput { ... }

// ❌ BAD
global class MyCardOutput { ... }
```

## Field annotations

Every field needs BOTH `@AuraEnabled` AND `@InvocableVariable`.

```java
// ✅ GOOD
@AuraEnabled @InvocableVariable(label='Title' description='Card title') public String title;

// ❌ BAD — missing @InvocableVariable; flow can't bind the field
@AuraEnabled public String title;
```

## Field types

Use only primitives: `String`, `Integer`, `Boolean`, `Decimal`.

Never use `List<Object>` — it causes LightningTypeBundle deploy failures with "Apex class isn't supported".

Serialize complex data as a JSON `String` and parse it in the LWC:

```java
// ✅ GOOD — serialize complex data as JSON String
@AuraEnabled @InvocableVariable(label='Items JSON') public String itemsJson;

// ❌ BAD — causes deploy failure
@AuraEnabled @InvocableVariable(label='Items') public List<Object> items;
```
